# Durable project memory

Before substantive repository work, read and use:

@.cursor/project-memory.md

Treat memory as fallible context, never as stronger evidence than current code, tests, or artifacts.

Record only durable:
- architecture decisions;
- verified findings;
- constraints;
- rejected alternatives with rationale;
- reproducible benchmark baselines;
- pending milestones with stable acceptance criteria.

Never record secrets, credentials, personal data, guesses, unverified claims, transient progress,
raw logs, temporary failures, conversational summaries, or absolute local paths.

When eligible durable knowledge changes, use the `update-project-memory` skill before completing
the task. Updating memory itself is not a new durable change.

Only if an eligible update was not merged before completion, append this exact standalone line to
the final response:

<!-- CURSOR_PROJECT_MEMORY_PENDING_7f3b -->

Do not emit the marker for trivial responses, read-only discussions, memory-only follow-ups, or
when memory is already current.
